index 0000000000..5d6cd35b39
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-transporter-bridge-20260907/NO_GO_DISCIPLINE_CHECKLIST.md
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+N1: Precise finite matrix-unitarity theorem only; no fabricated five-family or retained-authority claim.
+N2: Prospective contracts, original raw and R0 check strengthening preserved.
+N3: Actual Haar carrier, covariance, cutoff and Hamiltonian are explicit.
+N4: Exact57matrix finite witness supports but does not prove all-R statements.
+N5: Five literal scopes, TOTAL17, strict CLI, source SHA, finite JSON, positive RSS and180s/180MiB guards.
+N6: R>=1 energy bounds, distinct links, cutoff-ready input and unnormalized accepted output explicit.
+N7: No kinetic-form transfer from norm convergence, no general quantum-link exclusion.
+N8: Root and primary mathematical reviews PASS; canonical port/integration pending.
diff --git a/.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-transporter-bridge-20260907/NO_GO_LEDGER.md b/.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-transporter-bridge-20260907/NO_GO_LEDGER.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..8ab1e48fc0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-transporter-bridge-20260907/NO_GO_LEDGER.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+First trace cannot contradict a traceless Cartan generator; trace square does. Exact covariance alone is allowed. R0 has zero energy denominator and is excluded from energy bounds. Initial R0 finite assertion was tautological and replaced by literal vacuum block; both versions retained. Repeated-link projection commutation is not justified. Norm convergence does not control unbounded kinetic energy. No manufactured attempted families.
diff --git a/.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-transporter-bridge-20260907/OPPORTUNITY_QUEUE.md b/.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-transporter-bridge-20260907/OPPORTUNITY_QUEUE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..e9185a52a1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-transporter-bridge-20260907/OPPORTUNITY_QUEUE.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+Further finite hardware static-source upper bounds require kinetic-form approximation or an independently constructed finite trial. Repeated-link paths and inputs outside cutoff need separate estimates. No claim of an implemented dilation or state preparation.
