+# Root41 verification cold review
+
+PASS for ROOT_DERIVATION.md SHA82081e42d05de246e5ca4e1cb1f53d6236298259e7ba6e1e5cbbedf60e6a323c. Read the full proof after independently reviewing native90f8a663. Root transparently records exposure to the stronger path-bound summary; this is not portrayed as blind discovery.
+
+The full pullback covariance uses g inverse in the correct order. The Cartan differentiation and trace-square contradiction are valid. Its optional torus-character argument follows by exponentiating UAU*=A+B with commuting A,B; finite character continuity keeps chi_rho nonzero near identity. No first-trace contradiction is asserted.
+
+The actual PW highest-column kernel and fusion-shell argument match the independently checked proof. ceil(3R²/4)=R²-floor(R²/4) gives the exact balanced-shell energy. The inverse-orientation statement follows from conjugate fusion and the corresponding conjugate witness. No finite quantum-link covariance prohibition is introduced.
+
+The distinct-link projector identity and sum of shell losses use only color-identity projectors commuting with other-link unitaries, not mutual commutation of transporter matrices. Thus the total initial path-energy bound is valid with arbitrary entanglement. The stated exactness for all interior inputs follows from zero shell loss, including coherences. Repeated visits remain excluded.
+
+Normalization formulas are correct: normalized overlap sqrt(q), squared vector distance2(1-sqrt(q)), and one-half-convention pure-state trace distance sqrt(1-q). The note correctly distinguishes this from unbounded-energy expectation control and does not import the block38 energy trial into finite hardware. No correction requested.
