+This block proves a finite-carrier obstruction to exact fundamental transporter matrix unitarity together with exact endpoint covariance. For the actual full-irrep Peter–Weyl cutoff, covariance survives and the unitarity defect has norm one, supported on the top representation shell. A separate energy-dependent estimate controls initially retained states along distinct-link paths, including color/reference entanglement.
+
+The obstruction does not rule out finite gauge-covariant quantum-link models. Path outputs remain unnormalized until success weight is included, repeated-link paths are excluded, and norm approximation is not used to infer an unbounded kinetic-energy expectation. No hardware compiler or native cutoff selection is claimed.
+
+The reviewed source and runner retain their exact bytes. The live canonical cache contains 17 checks of the actual R=1 Haar multiplication compression on 19 link states and three colors. It is finite evidence for the analytical all-R proof. The original weak R0 check and its literal vacuum-compression correction remain in the packet, together with independent reviews and disclosed prior candidate exposure.
+
+Stacked on #8030. [Theorem](docs/GAUGE_WILSON_FINITE_TRANSPORTER_UNITARITY_PW_DEFECT_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-07.md), [runner](scripts/gauge_wilson_finite_transporter_pw_defect_check_2026_09_07.py), [handoff](.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-transporter-bridge-20260907/HANDOFF.md), [trace](.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-transporter-bridge-20260907/TRACE_GATE.md), [imports](.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-transporter-bridge-20260907/ASSUMPTIONS_AND_IMPORTS.md), [validation](.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-transporter-bridge-20260907/FINAL_VALIDATION.md).
+
