+# Block41 prospective exact transporter/cutoff bridge
+
+2026-09-07. Root exposed the Cartan-trace and highest-weight cutoff candidates before this contract. No completed root proof or new calculation has been read/run.
+
+Targets: (1) precise finite-dimensional obstruction to a matrix-unitary fundamental transporter with exact continuous SU3 endpoint covariance; only a Cartan subgroup is needed and pullback order/sign must be explicit. (2) actual full-irrep P_R cutoff of Haar multiplication: contraction defect D_R=I-U_R*U_R, shell support, norm1 via highest-weight input, exact interior action; (3) energy-priced state bounds and a simple distinct-link path bound, retaining color entanglement and avoiding a false operator-norm limit. R=0 and R>=1 domains must be distinguished.
+
+Potential failure points: a mere trace of the generator may vanish; covariance sign/group order; all three U_i1 U_11^R components must belong to the claimed irrep; finite truncation cannot be inferred from a generic quantum-link model; product path errors may need square-root-sum rather than an unjustified telescoping sum; energy estimates require the correct shell threshold. No claim against exact gauge covariance alone, dynamical finite quantum links, or low-energy approximation. No claim that block38's exact unitary trial identity automatically survives projection.
+
+Read primary quantum-link papers hep-lat/9609042 and2107.09335 for scope/prior art; mathematics must be derived directly. No repo edits. Any finite checks get a separate prospective fixture before execution.
