+# Independent block41 cold review
+
+PASS for native DERIVATION.md SHA90f8a663d06e9168cca60bd4e98fd5125d98a6f0cd284f45ced696cc5c126cb7. Full proof read independently. No source or integration worktree edits.
+
+The left pullback convention is correct: rho(g)f(x)=f(g^-1x) gives rho(g) mathsf U rho(g)^*=g^-1 mathsf U. For a Cartan subgroup the stated differential identity is therefore[Qbar,U]=-Tbar U. Under matrix unitarity it implies UQbarU*=Qbar+Tbar. Finite trace of squares produces dim(H)Tr(T²)>0 because the mixed tensor trace contains Tr(T)=0. This avoids both the vacuous first-trace calculation and any nonabelian order reversal. The contradiction does not concern covariance alone or unitary dynamics generated by a finite Hamiltonian.
+
+The full-irrep PW projection commutes with both left/right endpoint actions. The shell defect identity follows exactly from compression of a unitary. Fundamental and conjugate fusion take the R-1 interior into cutoffR; positivity then removes cross-shell blocks and gives0<=D_R<=T_R for both orientations.
+
+The explicit kernel vector is valid. g11^R is the matrix coefficient between unit highest-weight vectors in Sym^R(C3), hence its Haar norm squared is1/d_(R,0). Multiplying by g_i1 preserves the completely symmetric right tensor input e1^(tensor(R+1)); its coefficient lies entirely in Sym^(R+1), even though its left tensor vector need not initially be written symmetrically. Projection onto that symmetric component cannot create lower irreps. Thus every color component is removed by P_R. The normalized input is annihilated by U_R, establishing norm-one defect for everyR, includingR0. There is no all-cutoff-input norm convergence.
+
+The balanced-shell energy denominator is exact: p²+pq+q²=R²-pq, maximized pq=floor(R²/4), so g=[R²-floor(R²/4)+3R]/a. R>=1 is essential. Tensoring arbitrary color/reference does not alter the spectral projection inequality. The output comparison is to an unnormalized compression, not a channel with hidden success normalization.
+
+The stronger total-path-energy bound is correct. For distinct links, each link's PW projector is identity on shared color and commutes with all other link multipliers. Reordering only these projectors establishes W_R=PWP without incorrectly commuting different shared-color U matrices. In the output leakage for a particular link e, later distinct-link unitaries cancel after commuting its leakage projector; the one-step shell bound applies to the intermediate input, and the shell projector commutes with all earlier different-link unitaries. The commuting-projection union inequality therefore bounds total loss by the SUM of INITIAL shell probabilities, hence by initial total path electric energy divided by g. No reset, product-state assumption or extra color factor appears. Repeated links genuinely fall outside this proof.
+
+The normalized accepted-state formula is also correct: overlap with the exact output is sqrt(p), so squared vector distance is2(1-sqrt(p))<=2(1-p). Here epsilon bounds squared loss, as explicitly stated. For mixed states purification gives the unnormalized error statement; no universal nonlinear mixed-state normalization identity is claimed. Nonnegative potential permits replacing path kinetic budget with a total Hamiltonian budget, but vector norm approximation alone does not control unbounded output energy.
+
+Primary quantum-link abstracts hep-lat/9609042 and2107.09335 were opened directly. Their finite-dimensional gauge-symmetric setting is compatible with the explicit exclusion of a general finite-quantum-link no-go. The note correctly limits its obstruction to exact matrix unitarity plus endpoint covariance. No blocking mathematical or scope correction identified.
