@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Root review of native block41
+
+2026-09-07 21:35UTC. PASS for conditional-support scope. Reviewed complete native DERIVATION.md SHA25690f8a663d06e9168cca60bd4e98fd5125d98a6f0cd284f45ced696cc5c126cb7. Root had read the author's result summary before constructing its own verification and does not claim blind independence.
+
+The Cartan trace-square obstruction has the correct pullback sign; a first-trace argument would indeed fail. The actual highest-weight input is a normalized PW coefficient, and multiplication with a common first-column vector lands entirely in the excluded symmetric irrep, giving an exact kernel at every R. Positivity makes the interior annihilation imply the full shell-supported operator inequality, and balanced labels minimize the shell energy with the stated floor formula.
+
+The sharper path estimate is valid. Shared color does not let distinct link matrices commute, but it DOES let every link cutoff and shell projector commute with every other-link matrix. This is precisely the commutation used. The projected product is P W P, and the commuting output-projector union bound controls its squared loss. Moving a single leakage projector across later unitary factors and the shell projector across earlier factors gives the sum of initial shell probabilities without an extra path-length factor. Distinct links, retained initial support, and total versus per-link energy budgets are correctly explicit. Conditioning is priced by its probability and is not presented as a deterministic unitary operation.
+
+The final paragraph correctly declines any transfer of unbounded kinetic expectation from norm convergence, any all-encoding obstruction, or any derivation of dynamics from the four axioms. Primary quantum-link prior art is acknowledged. The matrix checker is corroboration for R=1; the all-R theorem rests on the representation-theoretic argument, not extrapolation from that finite fixture. Ready for canonical port and normal repository verification, subject to preserving this scope.
